  <compounddef id="Cache-example" kind="example">
    <compoundname>Cache</compoundname>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Allocate aligned memory from system heap. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Allocate aligned memory from system heap<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>bytes</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Number of bytes to allocate </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>alignment</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Required alignment in bytes (must be power of 2) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>zeroed</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>If true, zero-initialize the allocated memory (default: false) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Expected&lt;void*&gt; containing pointer to aligned memory or error</para>
</simplesect>
Allocates memory aligned to the specified boundary. The alignment must be a power of 2. If alignment is 0, uses default_alignment_.</para>
<para>Implementation strategy:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>If alignment &lt;= max_align_t: uses operator new</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>If alignment &gt; max_align_t: uses posix_memalign (POSIX) or _aligned_malloc (Windows)</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="exception"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Never</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>throws (uses nothrow allocation)</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="retval"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Expected</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>with pointer on success (aligned to specified boundary) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Expected</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>with InvalidArgError if bytes is 0 </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Expected</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>with BadAllocError if allocation fails</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
line alignment <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="classcslt_1_1HeapAllocator" kindref="compound">cslt::HeapAllocator</ref><sp/>allocator;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Allocate<sp/>aligned<sp/>to<sp/>64-byte<sp/>cache<sp/>line</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>result<sp/>=<sp/>allocator.<ref refid="classcslt_1_1HeapAllocator_1a53a1b9b301c70c4ce6035075385317e7" kindref="member">alloc_aligned</ref>(4096,<sp/>64,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keyword">false</highlight><highlight class="normal">);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">if</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>(result.hasValue())<sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">void</highlight><highlight class="normal">*<sp/>ptr<sp/>=<sp/>result.<ref refid="classcslt_1_1Expected_1a5d4e95808d25a88c3e7b2935a654f92f" kindref="member">value</ref>();</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Verify<sp/>alignment</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>assert(</highlight><highlight class="keyword">reinterpret_cast&lt;</highlight><highlight class="normal">uintptr_t</highlight><highlight class="keyword">&gt;</highlight><highlight class="normal">(ptr)<sp/>%<sp/>64<sp/>==<sp/>0);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight></codeline>
